    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by the elite 87.42 score for **Yordan Alvarez**. He faces a soft matchup against Bieber (xERA 5.48), and with an elite xwOBA of 0.477, he remains our premier start. **Junior Caminero** (84.24) is nearly as dangerous; he benefits from a massive 18% boost due to the favorable SP matchup against Lorenzen and carries significant momentum. While **Christian Yelich** (74.32) faces a competent catcher, his 100% stolen base opportunity against Chandler and a strong platoon advantage keep him well within the elite tier. Conversely, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (63.09) and **Trea Turner** (66.07) are prioritized today specifically for their stolen base upside against Alvarez; despite the threat of a quick delivery or high-hold percentages, their speed is non-negotiable in our 5x5 pursuit.\n\nOur middle-infield depth remains challenged, as **Pedro Ramirez** (47.93) and **Jacob Gonzalez** (45.76) sit squarely in the marginal category. **Pedro Ramirez** holds a slight edge due to the park factors and switch-hitting versatility, while **Jacob Gonzalez** is hindered by an unfavorable batting order position. On the bench, our options are limited by off-days for **Caleb Durbin**, **Colt Keith**, and **Chase Meidroth**, leaving us without a high-floor pivot for the middle infield. We are effectively locked into the current lineup, as **Lars Nootbaar** remains unavailable, removing the need for a complex substitution debate today. Owners should monitor weather conditions for any late-breaking concerns, but otherwise, the path to gaining ground in SBs and counting stats relies heavily on the efficiency of **Trea Turner** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** at the top of their respective orders.",
